'''Jon Kolb''' (born August 30, 1947) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was an [[Tackle (gridiron football position)|offensive tackle]] and [[Center (gridiron football)|center]] for 13 seasons with the [[Pittsburgh Steelers]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL). He played [[college football]] for the [[Oklahoma State Cowboys football|Oklahoma State Cowboys]]. He was also an occasional [[strongman]] competitor in some of the early [[World's Strongest Man]] contests.
